# The build runs on Linux, this machine is Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Nothing
# executed by the workflow may ever be stored with CRLF: Linux would read the shebang
# as "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and stop with "bad interpreter". These lines make that
# impossible rather than merely true today.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf

# Fonts and images are binary. Never let end-of-line conversion touch them.
*.otf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
